{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":904,"output":901,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":262,"totalTokens":28109,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The function works correctly. Let me also test that the invalid base64 case returns a proper \"chain\" error instead of \"range\". Let me check the code again.\n\nActually, looking at the test output, the invalid base64 case returns \"range: expected 2 entries, got 1\" because the base64 decode fails and the function returns early with a \"chain\" error message but it's caught by the length check. Let me fix this.\n\nWait, looking at my implementation:\n```python\nfor i, entry_b64 in enumerate(entries_b64):\n    try:\n        entry_raw = base64.b64decode(entry_b64, validate=True)\n    except ValueError:\n        return f\"chain: entry {i} is not valid base64\"\n```\n\nBut the test shows it returns \"range: expected 2 entries, got 1\". That's because the invalid base64 string \"not valid base64!\" is still a string in the list, so the list length is 1, not 2. The length check happens before the base64 decode. That's actually correct behavior - if the list has wrong length, we report \"range\" first.\n\nLet me test with correct length but invalid base64."}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":904,"output":901,"cacheRead":26304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":262,"totalTokens":28109,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-093bf672-2709-4bc1-ada3-075e7b31e194","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport record as R\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\n\n# Test invalid base64 with correct length\nledger = '/tmp/test_orphan2'\nimport os, shutil, json\nshutil.rmtree(ledger, ignore_errors=True)\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(ledger, 'inbox'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(ledger, 'entries'))\n\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer', 'claim': 'test', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'r'}\n\n# Create first entry (plan)\ne1 = {'seq': 1, 'prev': None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': PLAN}\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nh1 = hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()\n\n# Create second entry (verdict)\nVERDICT = {'by': 'verifier', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': h1}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}\ne2 = {'seq': 2, 'prev': h1, 'kind': 'verdict', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': VERDICT}\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nh2 = hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()\n\npred = {'from_seq': 1, 'to_seq': 2, 'prev_sha256': None, 'head_sha256': h2}\n\n# Test invalid base64 with correct length\norphan_bad_b64 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode(), 'not valid base64!']}}\nprint('Invalid base64 (correct length):', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_bad_b64, pred))\n\n# Test non-canonical entry\nbad_entry = json.dumps({'seq': 1, 'prev': None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': PLAN}, indent=1).encode()\norphan_non_canonical = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(bad_entry).decode(), base64.b64encode(raw2).decode()]}}\nprint('Non-canonical entry:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_non_canonical, pred))\n\nshutil.rmtree(ledger)\nprint('All tests passed!')\n\""}}}}
