ries_b64`, invalid base64, non-canonical entries, and missing predicate fields\n\n### 3. Wired into `cmd_monitor`\nAdded a call to `_orphan_entries_problem` when processing explained orphans. If the function returns a problem string, it's added to the `bad` list and the orphan is not accepted as a valid explanation.\n\n### Tests\nAll 19 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` continue to pass."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":3864,"output":442,"cacheRead":35072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":108,"totalTokens":39378,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794568288270,"responseId":"gen-1794568288-AZUg3rpC2DGw48dexU91","rawStopReason":"stop","durationMs":8930,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
